    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0317" n="237" xml:id="pg237"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Mutual Guarantee (Locarno)/394:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-03-12T17:00:00-05:00">March 12, 1936—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>51. Your March 9, 11 p.m. I have conveyed your message to the President and he
                    asks me to express his appreciation for your suggestion and the spirit in which
                    it is offered and to say that we are following the developments closely and are
                    hopeful that the procedure provided for this situation will obviate any
                    necessity for drastic action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
